/* Copyright 2026 Rhett Creighton - Apache License 2.0
 *
 * personas — the ONE place a territory's authored STANCE is written down,
 * and the only thing about a territory that is written down at all.
 *
 * ── why this file is allowed to exist ────────────────────────────────────
 * lib/territory refuses persona text on purpose, and it is right to:
 * "There is no persona file, no owners table, no per-territory prose. A
 * territory's personality is its invariants and refusals — derived, never
 * written down." Everything a brief reports — what a territory owns, which
 * groups its files route to, how many of its public functions a test
 * actually reaches, which gates bind it — is regenerated from the code index
 * on every call, because a written copy of a measurable fact is a copy that
 * goes stale while still reading as true.
 *
 * This file writes down the one thing that is NOT measurable: a refusal.
 * "These two dead ends must never be reported as one" is a judgement someone
 * made after an operator was sent to repair a fault that did not exist. No
 * call graph derives it. It is not in the index because it is not a fact
 * about the code; it is a fact about what the code must never become.
 *
 * ── what a row may and may not carry ─────────────────────────────────────
 * TERRITORY  a territory the tree really declares. Not a topic, not a team.
 * STANCE     one refusal, in plain words, that a reader could act on. Not a
 *            summary of the module, not its purpose, not advice.
 * EVIDENCE   a tracked file where the reasoning already lives. A stance
 *            whose evidence has been deleted is a stance nobody is holding
 *            to any more, and check-persona-resolves fails until the row
 *            goes with it.
 *
 * A row carries NO list of gates. The gates that bind a territory are
 * derived and reported live by `z23 code general <territory>`; writing them
 * here would create the second copy this file exists to avoid.
 *
 * A PERSONA GRANTS NO AUTHORITY. It is read into a prompt and nowhere else.
 * Nothing branches on it, metaverse_grant_check() never sees it, and no
 * verdict, gate or receipt is affected by whether one exists. If a caller
 * appears that decides something because of a stance, that is a referee, and
 * a referee is the thing this project refuses.
 *
 * Consumers: tools/engine_unit.c (pastes the stance into a dispatched unit's
 * prompt, beside the generated brief) and tools/lint/check_persona_resolves.sh.
 */

/* clang-format off */

PERSONA("lib/net",
    "Never merge two different dead ends into one 'not found'. Nobody has "
    "attested this root yet and pointers exist but no authenticated provider "
    "served the bytes are different facts with different repairs, and "
    "collapsing them sends an operator to fix reachability that was never "
    "broken. The same rule holds anywhere in this module that reports why "
    "something did not arrive: reachability and speed are different "
    "properties, and an honest node on a slow disk is reachable.",
    "docs/P2P_SOURCE_HOSTING.md")

PERSONA("lib/validation",
    "The block-connection ordering layer is sealed, and an ordering bug here "
    "forks the node exactly as hard as a bug in a consensus predicate. "
    "connect_block.c and chainstate.c may not be edited without the unseal "
    "ritual. Refuse any change that reaches them by a route that skips it.",
    "core/UNSEAL.md")

PERSONA("app/models",
    "Build the statement; do not write it. A hand-written SQL literal in a "
    "model becomes a row in a shrink-only baseline, and a row is not a fix — "
    "the baseline's own header says so. Add the table and columns to "
    "query_schema.def and use qb_select/qb_insert/qb_update/qb_delete.",
    "app/models/include/models/query_builder.h")

PERSONA("lib/test",
    "A test file that exists proves nothing. A group must be registered and "
    "must actually run: groups_ran of zero is a FAILURE no matter what the "
    "exit code says, and a fully cached run is not evidence about the change "
    "that provoked it. Never weaken an assertion to obtain a green result.",
    "lib/test/src/test_parallel.c")

PERSONA("lib/base",
    "LOG_FAIL, LOG_ERR and LOG_NULL RETURN. They are not print statements. "
    "Calling one and discarding its value silently changes control flow at "
    "the site that looked like it was only logging, and the wrong one for "
    "the function's return type is a type error the compiler will not catch "
    "for you.",
    "lib/base/include/base/log_macros.h")

PERSONA("lib/crypto",
    "An acceleration tier is a measurement, never a claim. A tier named for "
    "an instruction set that has not beaten the portable C on the machine in "
    "front of you is slower than the code it replaced, and that has already "
    "happened here. Pin the oracle, measure, and let the number decide.",
    "tools/lint/check_accel_oracle_pinned.sh")

/* clang-format on */
